tacks of  missile attacks of long distance through  that is still very much there yesterday  evening we heard a big explosion in the  downtown not far from our hotel and the  air raid sirens only came on about three  four minutes after itself and it's so  difficult to really tell when these  things are coming and they're coming  from such a short distance that the  systems here just can't really give  anyone a feeling of safety or you know  the real chance to get to a position  where they can you know be protected  from damage so it is a very edgy  situation in a city that doesn't really  quite know yet whether to believe uh  that the situation is genuinely safer  and whether it's gonna have time to go  back to some kind of normality and Nick  I believe you've been to the Border  region with Russia north of hakive where  Russian troops only pulled out a matter  of days ago uh tell us more about what  you saw  well this was uh an area that is as you  mentioned they're so close to the border  and where you can still hear artillery  fire pretty much every 10-15 minutes  those battles are still going on there  and people the people who had remained  in those Villages were kind of Dazed and  kind of shocked to see Outsiders they'd  have been cut off from the outside world  or at least from kharkiven from Ukraine  control territory for six months so the  Russian army basically turned up there  within the first few hours of this war  and people there talking about  rebuilding their houses time and time  again uh one older woman we spoke to had  just about rebuilt her roof when just a  couple of days before the Ukrainian  Force came back her house was basically  destroyed and she's now trying to work  out where she's going to spend the  winter people telling us of being taken  to uh sellers to being being mistreated  by the Russian authorities because they  have family ties to people serving in  the Ukrainian Army one man we saw were  just recovering some medals that belong  to relatives Ukrainian army medals that  he'd hidden to make sure that the  Russians didn't know about quite how  illustrious his relative's career had  been people who had disappeared who  still haven't been found or heard of for  months and we even saw the what we were  told were the remains of some Ukrainian  soldiers who died there pretty much  early on in this War and who the Russian  authorities hadn't buried a censor so  that the Russian forces there had left  in great haste uh bits of tech uh  armored vehicles dumped paperwork even  we saw a drawing from seemingly the  child of one of the Russian soldiers  there sent to the father who was serving  in Ukraine with that Zed symbol that  we've seen on all those Russian troop  troop cars so a real sense that this was  an area that really was abandoned yet  great haste and there's definitely the  suspicion from lots of people on the  ground there are still Russian forces  Russian soldiers hiding in abandoned  houses who just basically didn't manage  to get out in time and are now trying to  find some way of getting out without  being caught  that was DW's Nick Connelly reporting  from the Ukrainian city of hakif
 

